Z||000000||AL||12-09-1999||09:22 PM||||<BR>OK HERE IT IS,I HAVE A 86GT,I USE TO HAVE THE FAN RUNNING ALL THE TIME .IT HAD A WIRE CONNECTED FROM THE RELAY TO THE FAN SO WHEN YOU TURN THE CAR ON  IT CAME ON ALSO.WELL I DISSCONECTED IT AND CHECKED IF THE FAN WOULD COME ON AUTOMATICALLY, AND IT DOES, BUT WHEN I DRIVE I GET A CODE 32,BUT WHEN I PUT THE WIRE BACK IN AND THE FAN RUNS ALL THE TIME I DON'T GET THIS OR ANY CODE. I EVEN SWITHCHED THE EGR VALVE AND IT COMES ON WHEN THIS WIRE ISN'T CONNECTED. SO WHAT DO YOU THINK IT COULD BE.||||reg||1
Z||000001||kornholio||12-09-1999||09:50 PM||||Your EGR solenoid might be shot.  I kept getting code 32 even after I changed my EGR valve and tube.  So I changed the solenoid and I haven't gotten code 32 since.||||reg||1
Z||000002||AL||12-10-1999||12:25 AM||||how much for the solenoid? and did you get it from the dealer or autoparts?||||reg||1
Z||000003||mshill||12-10-1999||02:42 AM||||I get code 32 intermittently.  It seems to only do it when I have driven for more than 10 minutes above 65 MPH.  And lately only when climbing a long hill (ie. going up I80 from Sacramento to Reno).  I have blown through all the vacuum lines to/from the EGR soleniod and valve.  I don't know what to do next, but it came on over the weekend once.<BR>||||reg||11
Z||000004||kornholio||12-10-1999||11:50 AM||||Al,<BR>I got my EGR solenoid from a discount parts store called Car Quest.  Paid $132 Canadian.  The dealer wanted $200 for the EGR solenoid!<P>mshill,<BR>The problem you described is EXACTLY the same problem I had about 2 months ago.  I changed the EGR solenoid and it fixed the code 32.||||reg||1
